=t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401068 1072 #uuid "16fc9f31-33f6-5972-9529-3afa5f1e1dc8" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401068 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-1}{1+0} \\\\  & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401070 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401071 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401072 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401073 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401074 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1077 "selection" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401074 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401069 1080 #uuid "4182a726-9587-5280-b0ae-9a47c4e9e265" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401070 1081 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401070 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401070 1084 #uuid "bead1cb0-40bc-5682-8aea-b1306552b221" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401071 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533484 175921