\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401077 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401078 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401079 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401080 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401081 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1077 "selection" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401079 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401076 1080 #uuid "afbc7c1c-c03b-5382-bd6b-5a9beec491d4" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401077 1081 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401077 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401077 1084 #uuid "b60199c4-dc25-5568-af40-de39cd26589d" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401078 1081 "\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401078 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401078 1084 #uuid "41c812bd-cb3b-5fc5-aef0-fb585602e943" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401079 1081 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401079 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401079 1084 #uuid "ae37cc4a-dbda-5fe8-9ffa-a6b2a950bdbf" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401080 1081 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401080 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401080 1084 #uuid "a5fc02f7-9666-528e-9191-ebdcde2135fe" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401081 1081 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401081 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401081 1084 #uuid "3ea8ed64-c406-5164-b57d-847952b47323" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401082 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401083 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401082 1069 "q-15692" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401082 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401082 1071 "![](images/18/185393f07b920bf9b72799f1c17c4245017b500ff1ca92a0104fe95ce621bde4.png)\n\nFind the $y$-intercepts of the circle $(x-2)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=9,$ shown above." 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401082 1072 #uuid "b39c00d5-06a8-557a-8fa0-abcc975f62c0" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401082 1074 "We must have $x=0$ at the $y$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (0-2)^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ 4+(y-4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =9-4 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =5 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm \\sqrt{5} \\\\ y & =4\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts occur at the points $(0,4-\\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,4+\\sqrt{5}).$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401083 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401084 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401083 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401085 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401083 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401086 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401083 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401087 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401083 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401088 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401083 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401083 1077 "selection" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401083 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401088 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401083 1080 #uuid "62252cab-6046-5d37-8592-a5f805f44339" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401084 1081 "$(0,4-\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,4+\\sqrt{3})$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401084 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401084 1084 #uuid "d256b930-0dee-50c4-bd81-41d64217fa7f" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401085 1081 "$(0,6-\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,6+\\sqrt{3})$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401085 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401085 1084 #uuid "2759b4ff-6fe0-5744-9043-700096ff43f0" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401086 1081 "$(0,5-\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,5+\\sqrt{3})$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401086 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401086 1084 #uuid "0e3a7f86-7353-5871-ab3c-151f2b4eb6c7" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401087 1081 "$(0,5-\\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,5+\\sqrt{5})$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401087 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401087 1084 #uuid "4fc673dc-55ce-532c-a658-37120012f1ee" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401088 1081 "$(0,4-\\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,4+\\sqrt{5})$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401088 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401088 1084 #uuid "01d470c7-780c-5f9a-a462-fc902c6b68dd" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401089 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401090 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401089 1069 "q-156978" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401089 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401089 1071 "The vector-valued function $r(y,\\theta )$ parametrizes the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $x={sin}^{2}⁡y$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis for $y\\in [0,\\pi ].$ Which of the following could be $r?$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401089 1072 #uuid "428cd283-358d-5b3a-86aa-024fc5c3885c" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401089 1074 "![](images/be/be6fb27c0d050a7007e9f4a0d526daaff40b8f7d01f20c63ac8cc00074121f28.png)\n\n \n\nA point $(x,y,z)$ on the surface generated by rotating the graph of $x=f(y)$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis has the position vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨f(y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y,\\,f(y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,y\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta =[0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $x=f(y)={sin}^{2}⁡y\\ge 0$ for all $y\\in [0,\\pi ].$\n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\nr(y,\\theta )=⟨{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,y\\in [0,\\pi ],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401091 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401092 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401093 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401094 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401090 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401095 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401090 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401090 1077 "selection" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401090 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401094 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401090 1080 #uuid "4f2a13be-e010-5c10-884d-b42e9a33ee3c" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401091 1081 "⟨{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401091 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401091 1084 #uuid "2bbc1cc8-8336-57ba-beda-f232f5e9222e" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401092 1081 "⟨y,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401092 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401092 1084 #uuid "cd7b05bc-51cf-52c8-a8de-4a77f3929ff0" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401093 1081 "⟨{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,2\\pi y,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401093 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401093 1084 #uuid "56289067-d38c-5f93-8493-5a4b64b6dbc7" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401094 1081 "⟨{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401094 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401094 1084 #uuid "b49fe862-0b93-571b-b320-daffcc013018" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401095 1081 "⟨y,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401095 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401095 1084 #uuid "94ddc772-4e3c-53f3-95c3-4e3a3d691c6d" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401096 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401097 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401096 1069 "q-157052" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401096 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401096 1071 "$$\n\\boxed{}\\,x=\\boxed{}\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the matrix equation above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401096 1072 #uuid "f81ecce3-b49e-5261-aee2-21f0b16a1f87" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401096 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ R\\,\\,x & ={Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are $R$ and ${Q}^{T}.$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401098 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401099 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401100 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401101 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401097 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401102 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401097 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401097 1077 "selection" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401097 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401101 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401097 1080 #uuid "474be29c-51a5-5850-8515-5dee1fd67caa" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401098 1081 "$R$ and $Q$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401098 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401098 1084 #uuid "f67bd72e-fdc1-5a03-8447-bfd09a70f376" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401099 1081 "$Q$ and $R$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401099 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401099 1084 #uuid "01a67471-d12d-5153-bc2d-d06208bd68e9" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401100 1081 "$A$ and $R$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401100 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401100 1084 #uuid "c4dbeaf3-ad0e-5cbe-a0fc-7d2689833b25" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401101 1081 "$R$ and ${Q}^{T}$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401101 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401101 1084 #uuid "66035904-de9d-5004-9133-f65b6dd564b6" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401102 1081 "$Q$ and ${R}^{T}$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401102 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401102 1084 #uuid "f8434c0c-cb29-5697-82e4-05952a54d5fc" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401103 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401104 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401103 1069 "q-158036" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401103 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401103 1071 "$$\nx=\\boxed{}\\,\\boxed{}\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401103 1072 #uuid "d32f936e-03bc-5f70-a00c-2926fd51fe56" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401103 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & =\\,\\,\\,{R}^{-1}\\,\\,{Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of t