94139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401199 1069 "q-160608" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401199 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401199 1071 "![](images/33/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=v-{u}^{2},\\,y=u+v.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{2}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401199 1072 #uuid "5f849a8c-d5a9-5291-8dbf-bee7c6e87ffd" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401199 1074 "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{2}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{2},$ we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(v-{u}^{2},\\,u+v) \\\\  & =(v-{1}^{2},\\,1+v) \\\\  & =(v-1,\\,v+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{2}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=v-1,\\,y=v+1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t-1,\\,y(t)=t+1,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(-1,1)$ and $(0,2)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](images/f3/f304c409cfc62de3d296690c0acd2cec5b9726c03d8a196ed69de36d8ebbefd2.png)" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401200 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401201 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401200 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401202 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401200 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401203 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401200 1075 #