 [17592186401287 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401287 1084 #uuid "f3a89ced-7070-57be-88cf-4d4b894bd3f7" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1068 #edb/ref 17592186401289 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1069 "q-161816" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u} \\\\ {e}^{u+w} \\\\ uv+w\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1072 #uuid "fc380b3f-d92e-5c45-8651-fac240787b92" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401288 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)={e}^{u},\\,y(u,v,w)={e}^{u+w},\\,z(u,v,w)=uv+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & ={e}^{u+w} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & ={e}^{u+w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =u & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u} & 0 & 0 \\\\ {e}^{u+w} & 0 & {e}^{u+w} \\\\ v & u & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u}|\\begin{aligned}0 & {e}^{u+w} \\\\ u & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u}(0-u{e}^{u+w}) \\\\  & =-u{e}^{2u+w}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ -u{e}^{2u+w} & =0 \\\\ u & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u=0$ defines the plane $u=0,$ i.e., $vw$-plane." 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401290 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401291 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401292 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401293 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401294 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1077 "selection" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1079 #edb/ref 17592186401290 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401289 1080 #uuid "175d9200-8100-5e54-b984-b7451df1967c" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401290 1081 "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401290 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401290 1084 #uuid "b76c85a4-c631-5c36-941d-c14613479d8a" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401291 1081 "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $w=-2{v}^{2}.$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401291 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401291 1084 #uuid "10a3627e-14c0-553d-8005-b8e65337d0b7" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401292 1081 "The critical points lie on the plane $2u+v+w=0.$" 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401292 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533484 17592186045585 true] [17592186401292 1084 #uuid "b1ffd8d2-f852-57f7-9970-8454309f0281" 13194139533484 17592186045585